glegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/leaflet-binding/leaflet.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;script src=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/leaflet-providers/leaflet-providers_1.9.0.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;script src=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/leaflet-providers-plugin/leaflet-providers-plugin.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;link href=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/HomeButton/home-button.css&#34; rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; /&gt;&#xA;&lt;script src=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/HomeButton/home-button.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;script src=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/HomeButton/easy-button-src.min.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;script src=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/clipboard/setClipboardText.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;link href=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/mapviewCSS/mapview-popup.css&#34; rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; /&gt;&#xA;&lt;link href=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/mapviewCSS/mapview.css&#34; rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; /&gt;&#xA;&lt;script src=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/kePrint/kePrint.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;link href=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/lightable/lightable.css&#34; rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; /&gt;&#xA;&lt;script src=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/kePrint/kePrint.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;link href=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/lightable/lightable.css&#34; rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; /&gt;&#xA;&lt;script src=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/kePrint/kePrint.js&#34;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;link href=&#34;https://bloglegacy.insileco.io/rmarkdown-libs/lightable/lightable.css&#34; rel=&#34;stylesheet&#34; /&gt;&#xA;&lt;br/&gt;&#xA;&lt;h1 id=&#34;online-ecology&#34;&gt;Online ecology&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let’s imagine that we are interested in a species in a given area and wish to&#xA;know as much as possible about it. But, you can’t go out in the field because&#xA;funding is running short. What we do have, however, is a certain knowledge of&#xA;the open data science tools that are at our disposal. In a series of post&#xA;about online ecology, we will find out exactly just how far these tools allow&#xA;us to delve into the ecology of the species that interest us.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
